<report>
<title>Correlation meta-analysis</title>
<table>
<tr><th>Study</th><th>Size</th><th>@stat</th><th colspan="2"><ci>Approximate @{pc:round2}% CI</ci></th><th></th></tr>
<block name="studies"><tr><td>@st</td><td>@{n:roundu}</td><td>@{y:roundu}</td><td><ci>@{from:roundu}</ci></td><td><ci>@{to:roundu}</ci></td><td>@lb</td></tr></block>
</table>

<table>
<tr><th>Stratum</th><th>Standardized effect</th><th>Variance</th><th colspan="3">% Weights (fixed, random, size)</th><th></th></tr>
<block name="studies"><tr><td>@st</td><td>@{yi:roundu}</td><td>@{vi:roundu}</td><td>@{wt:roundu}</td><td>@{dwt:roundu}</td><td>@{nwt:roundu}</td><td>@lb</td></tr></block>
</table>

<p><u>Hedges-Olkin fixed effects</u><br />
Pooled @stat_fixed = @{rmh:roundu} (<ci>@{pc:round2}% CI = @{from_fixed:roundu} to @{to_fixed:roundu}</ci>)<br />
Z (test correlation differs from 0) = @{z:roundu}  <pval>@{p_fixed:pval}</pval></p>

<p><u>Non-combinability of studies</u><br />
Cochran Q = @{qc:roundu}  (df = @df)  <pval>@{xp:pval}</pval><br />
Moment-based estimate of between studies variance = @{tausq:roundu}<br />
I&#xb2; (inconsistency) = @{isq:round1}% (<ci>@{pc1:round1}% CI = @{llisq:round1}% to @{ulisq:round1}%</ci>) </p>

<p><u>Hedges-Olkin random effects</u><br />
Pooled @dsstat = @{dsrr:roundu} (<ci>@{pc:round2}% CI = @{dsll:roundu} to @{dsul:roundu}</ci>)<br />
Z (test correlation differs from 0) = @{dz:roundu}  <pval>@{dp:pval}</pval></p>

<p><u>Bias indicators</u></p>
<block name="bias">
<p>Begg-Mazumdar: Kendall's @{tau:roundu}@{warnTooFewStrata}  <pval>@{p2:pval}</pval><br />
Egger: bias = @{a:roundu} (<ci>@{pc_egger:round2}% CI = @{cl:roundu} to @{cu:roundu}</ci>)  <pval>@{p:pval}</pval></p>
</block>

<p><u>Schmidt-Hunter</u><br />
Weighted mean correlation (95% CI): @{wmr:roundu} (<ci>@{wmr_lcl:roundu} to @{wmr_ucl:roundu}</ci>)<br />
Z (test correlation differs from 0) = @{wmr_z:roundu} <pval>@{wmr_p:pval}</pval></p>

<p>Observed variance across studies: @{var_r:roundu}<br />
Variance due to sampling error: @{var_e:roundu}<br />
Variance in the population correlations: @{var_p:roundu}<br />
95% Credibility interval for weighted mean correlation: @{wmr_crll:roundu} to @{wmr_crul:roundu}</p>

<p>Indicators of homogeneity/heterogeneity:</p>
<table>
<tr><td>1.</td><td>Residual standard deviation (should be smaller than 1/4 WMC: @{wmr4:roundu}): @{sres:roundu}</td></tr>
<tr><td>2.</td><td>Percent of observed variance accounted for by sampling error (should be at least 75%): @{percvar:roundu}</td></tr>
<tr><td>3.</td><td>Chi-square test of heterogeneity: @{het_x2:roundu} <pval>@{het_p:pval}</pval></td></tr>
</table>
</report>
